                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1]A Surprisingly Fun Little Adventure[/h1]\n\nMan, this game was an interesting one.\n\nNot the best game I've ever played, but definitely not the worst either.\n\nI liked the atmosphere, the story, and after the first few levels, even the gameplay.\n\nI'll keep this short.\n\n[h1]Gameplay[/h1]\n\n[list]\n[*]Action-adventure game where you control two characters: your main character and an ally.\n\n[*]You can switch between them whenever you want. The main character is more of a tank, while the companion fills the DPS role.\n\n[*]Your companion is surprisingly intelligent. He can carry his own weight and rarely needs babysitting.\n\n[*]You kill stuff, complete quests, explore, and earn XP. XP is used to buy skills and upgrades. You start off pretty weak, but once you invest into the right skills, you eventually evolve into an absolute power demon.\n\n[*]The gameplay can get repetitive, but it's simple and I never found it frustrating or overly challenging.\n[/list]\n\n[h1]Graphics[/h1]\n\n[list]\n[*]The models and environments remind me of Counter-Strike 1.6, just with better textures. Honestly, I found them pretty charming.\n\n[*]Character faces can look a bit wonky. The concept art shown in the menus sometimes barely resembles the actual in-game models.\n\n[*]Animations are a little janky, but never bad enough to ruin the experience.\n[/list]\n\n[h1]Music[/h1]\n\n[list]\n[*]Some of the tracks are actually pretty good.\n\n[*]Too bad the looping occasionally breaks or starts acting randomly.\n[/list]\n\n[h1]Story[/h1]\n\n[list]\n[*]The story does a lot of the heavy lifting.\n\n[*]There are some decent plot twists and the overall premise is interesting.\n\n[*]It's a fun adventure through that period's historical events.\n[/list]\n\n[hr][/hr]\n\nOverall, it's a decent game.\n\nI genuinely had fun with it, even if it dragged on a bit longer than necessary towards the end.\n\n[quote]And don't question how the Templars managed to build  fire traps with infinite supply of flammable material .\n\nJust go with it.\n\nMaybe gas was free back then.[/quote]\n\n[b]Recommended.[/b]",
